From ee1d62271fed8ddbb6ab8392be1b33104f813e9d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chaton <definitelyfrenchname@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 10:24:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] cps2w: the vsavjw catalogue entry re-pointed to merged-m18
 (14z-144)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

jtframe's .rom builder locates every zip member by CRC32 and by nothing else
(mra2rom.go:163-172, no name fallback), so the machine entry must name the
CRCs of the actual build or the MRA produces no .rom at all. Regenerated from
build/m3b_merged26/rompath/vsavjw.zip (sha1 7150c623) by tools/gen_vsavjw_xml.py
in the consuming tree; --check now reports the catalogue matches the build.

THREE members moved, and they are the M18 delta exactly:
  vsw.41   41e34588 -> c6fe6e5e   the program extension — the Donovan/Jedah
                                  capture-scope fix, EXACTLY TWO BYTES
                                  (logical word 0d88 -> 0b30 at blob offset
                                  0x1E of throw_victim_keyframes)
  vsw.33m  263cb145 -> bcb4d72c   group-C glyphs, the M17 -> M18 mark
  vsw.37m  2a70f185 -> 70df1050   likewise

No RTL, no cfg, no core change: doc/mame.xml only. cores/cps1, cores/cps2 and
cores/cps15 remain byte-untouched.
---
 doc/mame.xml | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

